        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_39952269cb174b53b72d48785aeaf6e0",
      "statement": "celld opens two HTTP listeners: the public Worker listener (--listen) and the internal peer/operator listener (--internal-listen) that defaults to 127.0.0.1:0; the public listener reserves only /.well-known/celld/health and the internal listener returns 404 for unknown paths rather than passing them to the Worker.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L21-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64a705b6105962b15f3a010ead1d1f4fc1b6d931a0b466f0286bc632920209ac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bd5b382b4a264eec96022b7f56448ece",
      "statement": "The fleet HMAC authenticates peer-control and reserved-cell operator requests with a clock limit and replay protection, and the peer tunnel establishment request carries it so only a holder of the fleet secret can open a tunnel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L59-L77",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c44e39377c8734a1e520e2ecdff61100645113b920ade049ab1217245a466689:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b7f0a181ced0498d917db7184c2eb32e",
      "statement": "The clock window is two-sided (30 seconds) and replay retention must be at least the clock window, enforced as pure predicates in crates/logic/peer.rs so the replay hole cannot reopen.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L25-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:58abd41c53310c42ff3eec8caed852ca8a42ec7b5bb9d58e8bd66693905c5ad0:"
        },
        {
